  "result": "Done! I've added `addLine()` and `removeLine()` functions to modify draft invoices:\n\n**`addLine(invoice, { sku, qty })`** \u2014 Adds a new line to an invoice or increases qty if that SKU already exists. Returns ok(newInvoice) with the enriched line. Validates qty and sku like createInvoice, fails with NOT_DRAFT if invoice status isn't 'draft'.\n\n**`removeLine(invoice, sku)`** \u2014 Removes a line by SKU. Fails with:\n- `LINE_NOT_FOUND` if the SKU isn't on the invoice\n- `NO_LINES` if it would remove the last line\n- `NOT_DRAFT` if the invoice status isn't 'draft'\n\nAdded error codes: `NOT_DRAFT`, `LINE_NOT_FOUND`\n\nAdded 14 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Adding new lines and updating existing ones\n- All validation and error cases (qty, sku, status)\n- Non-mutation of input invoices\n- Integration with createInvoice\n- Combined usage of both functions\n\nAll 44 tests pass \u2713",
